> avg(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b) / 2
> wrap avg
wrap analysis of avg:
  a + b   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 16384 points, e.g. a=127, b=1
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> avg2(a: u8, b: u8) = (a & b) + ((a xor b) >> 1)
> wrap avg2
wrap analysis of avg2:
  (a & b) + ((a xor b) >> 1)   (u8)
      nuw holds
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 16256 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> equiv avg avg2
avg and avg2 differ at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1: 0 vs 128
> s(x: i8) = x * 2 + 1
> wrap s
wrap analysis of s:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  2x + 1   (i8)
      nuw holds
      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -64..63
  over all 256 points of the domain
> domain s
domain of s:
  x: i8, -128..127
  C assumes 2x + 1 does not overflow i8  (signed overflow)
  C assumes 2x does not overflow i8  (signed overflow)
  defined at 256 of 256 points
  C undefined behaviour at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
  over all 256 points of the domain
> dec(x: u8) = x > 0 ? x - 1 : 0
> wrap dec
wrap analysis of dec:
  x - 1   (u8)
      nuw holds
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=128
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> q(x: u8) = 100 / (x - 3)
> domain q
domain of q:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires x - 3 != 0  (in 100/(x - 3))
  defined at 255 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..2, 4..255
  undefined e.g. at x=3
  C undefined behaviour at 1 points, e.g. x=3
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range q
range of q -> u8:
  0..100   (20 distinct values)
  values: 0..12, 14, 16, 20, 25, 33, 50, 100
  fits in u7
  undefined at 1 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> h(x) = x^3 - 3x
> crit h
critical points of h:
  h' = 3x^2 - 3
  x ≈ -1: local maximum, h = 2
  x ≈ 1: local minimum, h = -2
  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)
> diff h
d/dx h = 3x^2 - 3
> range h
range of h:
  [-970, 970]   min at x ≈ -10, max at x ≈ 10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
> r(x) = log(x) / (x - 1)
> domain r
domain of r:
  x: real (default [-10, 10])
  requires x - 1 != 0  (in log(x)/(x - 1))
  requires x > 0
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in (0, 1)
    x in (1, 10]
    except x ≈ 1  (x - 1 = 0)
> c(x: real in -3..3) = |x| + x^2
> crit c
critical points of c:
  c' = sign(x) + 2x
  x ≈ 0: local minimum, c = 0
> seg(x: u8 in 0..20) = x < 5 ? 2x + 1 : x < 12 ? 11 : 40 - 2x
> crit seg
critical points of seg:
  piecewise-affine segments (consecutive x with a constant step):
    x in 0..5: seg = 2x + 1
    x in 5..11: seg = 11
    x in 11..12: seg = 5x - 44
    x in 12..20: seg = -2x + 40
  local extrema (where the step changes sign):
    x = 12: local maximum, seg = 16
> diff seg
forward difference over x: seg(x+1) - seg(x) = (x + 1 < 5 ? 2(x + 1) + 1 : x + 1 < 12 ? 11 : 40 - 2(x + 1)) - (x < 5 ? 2x + 1 : x < 12 ? 11 : 40 - 2x)
